    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on 3 February 2006, the erection of a side and rear loft extension and two roof lights, measuring 7.5m in depth, 3.773m width and 3.133m in perpendicular height on the side extension, and, a width of 5.798m, a depth of 2.788m and a height of 2.433m for the rear extension, was not lawful within the meaning of Section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reason:\r\n\r\nThe development exceeds the provisions of Schedule 2, Part 1, Class A of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995 because the proposal extends on a roof slope fronting a highway."
